It is now definite that I have played this game much too often.  Although
I didn't play for the week, I found myself dreaming about Nethack this
morning.  That's not so bad in itself, until you consider what my warped
mind is able to conjure.

Like always, I was playing a low-level character (4 or less) and as I
zipped around I picked up lots of stuff to identify later.  Every now
and then a perfectly normal-looking object has some magic attached to it.

At one point, I felt myself continually getting flamed, with current
and max hit points dropping.  Like I always do in a panic, I looked through
my inventory, where I found "a cursed -1 credit card of fire."  Effectively,
this item had the same effect as if you read a series of scrolls of fire.
Why my imagination chose to use a credit card is beyond me.  Anyway,
I dropped that item in a hurry.

The other magic item was a bit more useful and would probably be fun to
have: the Cape of Grandeur.  There is probably a better name, but this is
what my dream inventory told me it was called.  Wearing this cape allows
you to leap and lunge like all those Errol Flynn movies, making you quite
a bit harder to hit.  Also, you can attack a monster from two squares away,
with a lunge attack, ending up on some square nearer or past your opponent.
The drawback is that you also get minuses on your on To-Hit, which is a
real problem for a low-level character.  Even so, the improved AC more than
makes up for that.

Even if neither of these special items actually appears in the game, I'm sure
the Dev Team would have fun working from these ideas.  If ever I get more
inspiration from Altered States, I'll let you know.

